# Probe for destructure as a function parameter — item 20 of the test
# domain.  `fn foo([a, b]) { ... }` would let a function accept a
# 2-element list and bind its slots directly.  The H# parser's
# `function_declaration` only accepts IDENTIFIER params, so a `[` in
# the param list should raise a compile-time SyntaxError.
#
# Expected: COMPILE ERROR.  This probe exists only to confirm that.

fn sum_pair([a, b]) {
    return a + b;
}
print(sum_pair([3, 4]));
